\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O happy home where Thou art loved the dearest,
\par Thou loving Friend, and Saviour of our race,
\par And where among the guests there never cometh
\par One who can hold such high and honoured place!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O happy home where two in heart united
\par In holy faith and blessed hope are one,
\par Whom death a little while alone divideth,
\par And cannot end the union here begun!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O happy home whose little ones are given
\par Early to Thee, in humble faith and prayer,
\par To Thee, their Friend, who from the heights of heaven
\par Guides them, and guards with more than mother's care!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O happy home where each one serves Thee, lowly,
\par Whatever his appointed work may be,
\par Till every common task seems great and holy,
\par When it is done, O Lord, as unto Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O happy home where Thou art not forgotten
\par When joy is overflowing, full and free;
\par O happy home where every wounded spirit
\par Is brought, Physician, Comforter, to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Until at last, when earth's day's work is ended,
\par All meet Thee in the blessed home above,
\par From whence Thou camest, where Thou hast ascended,
\par Thy everlasting home of peace and love!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

